phase P11
title Persistence
description
    **Class:** not readily verifiable.

    **Kind:** verification-suite.

    **Goal:** the persistence area (@task.V3.T10) proven in the suite, then the persistence edge, write-ahead and the 
    Effect driver in `src/host/`.

    **Verified by:**

    - the area's suite: green on round 14, null 0 of N, every oracle killing its own mutants for the expected reason,
      reviewed, and audited by its own adversarial auditor (skill:policy-testing#audit-a-suite);
    - then the production module through the production adapter: that suite passes, with its coverage rows in
      @plan.Runtime's verification;
    - skill:check-task per Task; `nub run check` at zero.

    **One iteration:** the area's suite Task first (from its Spec, run on round 14 and the null runtime, its mutants, 
    the
    review, findings gathered by root cause); then its production Task, built test-first against the proven suite.
    When production and a case disagree, the Spec decides and the fix cites its rule.

    **Exit criteria:**

    - the area's suite is green on round 14, null-red, mutant-proven, reviewed and audited by its own auditor before the
      production module starts;
    - the production module then passes it, with its gates failing on a broken runtime.

    **False pass:** the production adapter doing work the runtime should; a case edited to pass.

    **Caught by:** mutants run against the production adapter, a review section on the adapter's role, and the audit.

    **Gates:**

    - falsify on both adapters (`packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`, each oracle's mutants file);
    - `nub run check`, which rejects a planted lint violation (`tools/lint-bomb/`).

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:**

    - a guarantee change or one that can't be met;
    - public entry-point names or a large public API change.

    **User's read:** each Spec revision, each changed expected result with its reason, the internal module layout, small
    public API calls.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:policy-verification (prove a suite; the coverage record);
    - skill:policy-testing (audit a suite; test first: module integration tests through the public interface, no unit
      tests of internals, and the scenarios that enforce each Invariant written before the code);
    - skill:to-spec for the area's Spec and skill:to-design per module;
    - skill:policy-convergence at the threshold; skill:review at the cadence;
    - skill:playbook-build (long runs), skill:execute-task, skill:check-task; skill:diagnose when a case fails
      unexplained.
tasks

    T46
        title       Backtest: does a search over the Spec model find the audit's protocol conflicts?
        status      open
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@task.V3.T45]
        description
            Run the model's search against the Specs as of `bcc2bbbb` (before the Invariant audit) and count which
            of the audit's 10 to 12 protocol conflicts it finds.

            **Why now:** the user will bring back TLA+ or another prover only if it helps; the advisor's Q4 says
            try TLC only if the search misses three or more.

            **Read first:** code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/advisor-answers-2026-11-11.md (Q4); 
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/invariant-audit-2026-11-11.md.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comment, with the found and missed conflicts.
        acceptance
            - each protocol conflict from the audit marked found or missed by the search;
            - a recommendation on TLC, per the three-miss rule.

    T10
        title       WriteAhead area complete
        status      open
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@task.V3.T5, @task.V3.T40, @task.V3.T45]
        description
            Cover @spec.WriteAhead's guarantee map, with a disk reader on the Port or the adapter.

            **Why now:** the Port has no disk reader yet (README, "Planned Port changes"), so no WriteAhead
            Invariant can be judged; @task.V3.T11 reads the same disk reader.

            **Read first:** code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/README.md (the WriteAhead rows of the
            guarantee map, and "Planned Port changes"), @spec.WriteAhead,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/port.ts#Port,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/world/storage.ts#makeStorage. A disk reader must not show
            internals: @spec.Conformance.R1.

            **Approach:** oracles `write-ahead` (the old oracle (h) against the storage host), `capture`,
            `persistence`; cases; the storage faults (failLate, plain-write failures, slow and failing loads,
            wipe, tear, corrupt); ported cases, verdict compare and carry rows.

            - **May change:** the Port, the suite's write-ahead area and storage host.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a disk reader that shows internals → caught by T4's Spec and the
              audit.
            - **Gates:** falsify; `nub run check`.
            - **Stops:** a guarantee change.
            - **User's read:** the Port change, Spec revisions.
        acceptance
            - Every WriteAhead Invariant has its oracle or case;
            - each oracle kills its listed mutants;
            - verdicts match the old suite's or each difference is logged.
    T19
        title       Persistence edge, write-ahead and the driver
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@task.V3.T18, @T10]
        satisfies   [@plan.Persistence.O1, @plan.Persistence.O2, @plan.Persistence.O3, @plan.Persistence.O6]
        description
            Build the persistence edge, write-ahead and the Effect driver in `src/host/` from @spec.WriteAhead.

            **Why now:** the core returns work as data; nothing runs it or writes records yet, so durability
            cannot be judged.

            **Read first:** @spec.WriteAhead, @spec.WriteAhead.I15 (which took the cut I16), @spec.WriteAhead.I17,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/README.md ("Planned Port changes": the disk reader).

            **Scope added** (the user, 2026-11-11, from
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/plan-task-coverage-2026-11-11.md): add an Invariant for
            WriteAhead R2: the KeyValueStore type rule and untyped missing storage (row Q02, an owed check;
            @plan.Persistence.O1).

            **Read first (added):** @plan.Persistence.O1.

            - **May change:** `src/`.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** durability judged from the runtime's report → caught by the disk
              reader.
            - **Gates:** the suite; falsify.
            - **Stops:** a guarantee change.
        acceptance
            - The WriteAhead area passes on production.
            - WriteAhead R2 has an Invariant with an oracle or case.
